# Probe and implementation separation

**No session both probes and implements** the same component. That hard split covers API-behavior probes and raw-format probes.

Two kinds of probing still differ in *what* they may capture, not in session splitting:

**API-behavior probes** call documented APIs on the Windows 10 22H2 guest and record status codes, return values, and user-visible output ([windows-capture.mdc](windows-capture.mdc)).

**Raw-format probes** capture bytes Windows writes below the API: raw disk sectors from the guest image, on-disk file system structures, registry hive files, or other persisted binary formats. They read the guest's disk image or files only—never Windows memory, binaries, or debugger output ([clean-room-symbols-and-debuggers.mdc](clean-room-symbols-and-debuggers.mdc)).

For either kind:

1. **Probe / spec session.** Designs and runs a versioned probe under `tavera/probes/` (layout in [tavera-probes.mdc](tavera-probes.mdc)), stores captures under `output/<module>/<probe-id>/`, and updates `tavera/specs/<module>/`. Every capture-backed statement cites that probe path and the capture (and marker). Resolves `open-items.md` entries per [tavera-specs-open-items.mdc](tavera-specs-open-items.mdc). Does **not** edit implementation code for that component (`drivers/`, related DLLs, etc.).
2. **Implementation session.** A new session that has not interpreted the raw captures (for raw-format work)—only the specs and the logs those specs cite. Implements from the specs and verifies with a differential probe (`DIFF ... END OK`) or the suite the specs name. If a fact is missing or unclear, adds an item to `tavera/specs/<module>/open-items.md` and does not infer the fact or run a new Windows probe in this session.

Name both sessions in the transparency note for the implementation commit.

```text
Right: probe session records NtQueryVolumeInformationFile statuses; later session implements from the cited spec/log
Right: probe-v1 dumps sectors after CreateFileW; spec cites probe-v1 and output/…; new session implements
Right: implementer opens NTFS-014 in open-items.md; spec/probe session runs probe-v2 and resolves the item
Wrong: same chat probes Windows and edits ntfs.sys for that behavior
Wrong: one session reads hex dumps of the guest disk and writes the driver struct
Wrong: overwriting probe-v1 after specs already cite it
Wrong: implementer invents a field because the spec was silent
```
